{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1469719-dtd-what-are-your-house-rules","id":1469719,"title":"DtD, What are your House Rules?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-06T05:06:30-08:00","id":1469719,"title":"DtD, What are your House Rules?","content":"This gameline has been out for a good amount of time and I find myself curious what twists or tweaks others have made to the game to fit their table best. What small, or not so small, changes have you implemented or seen others implement and how did it affect the game? Of course though, if I'm asking I should also provide what I have done to get the ball rolling.<br /> <br /> The following are a few small changes I've made for my own game out of personal preference:<br /> <br /> 1) Investigating a demon uses Investigation rather than the occult skill, as you investigate the inconsistencies that may surround a cover. Be it the limitations of whose memories are altered by pacts, the effects of low cover or other things someone looking close enough may notice.<br /> <br /> 2) As I've seen others do as well, I took a stab at changing the show of power exploit. First off it can only &quot;hold&quot; a number of abilities up to your primum. When you see an ability you may activate the exploit to &quot;record&quot; the effect rather than produce it. When recording an ability if you have no available capacity you may &quot;overwrite&quot; one of the previously recorded abilities. Then finally, if mimicking a mage's spell the mimicked effect is at minimum spell factors though the primary spell factor still applies its bonus, treating the demon as having arcana equal to the spell's rating. This is to enable the intent of the exploit only affectively achieving a single success on a powers activation.<br /> <br /> 3) Pacts that are unbalanced in favor of a mortal may attract angelic notice. For each point it is unbalanced in favor of the mortal the storyteller may roll one dice. On a success, the God-Macine takes notice and an angel or other agent of the god machine will investigate sometime in the next session/chapter. On an exceptional success the pactbound gains the surveilled condition. When the condition refers to cover, use the pactbound's integrity score instead. If the surveilled condition progresses to hunted, those hunting the pactbound are not seeking to kill them but rather kidnap and extract information regarding the unchained.<br /> <br /> 4) In regards to &quot;Pacts are usually permanent, lasting for as long as the contract exists and both parties live.&quot; Change [Both] to [Either]<br /> <br /> 5) Exiled may participate in &quot;Cover trading&quot; as detailed in Interface as though they were one of the unchained. Any details they purchase must immediately incorporated into their cover. It is called out in the story teller's guide that exiles lack the support of the god machine to restore their own cover as well as do not have access to pacts as demons do to maintain it themselves. This is primarily to give exiles clear motivation or benifit for cooperating with the unchained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T13:09:35-08:00","id":1469760,"title":"","content":"Been a while since I ran <b>Demon</b>, but I always capped the bonus on compromises you get for not using your forms at +5. It made the dice pool less unwieldy and a <i>tiny </i>bit more likely to fail. It also patches over an oddity that comes up where characters with Terrible Form are <i>really </i>good at handling partial transformation compromises.<br /> <br /> (Aaaand now I'm reading through the core and really want to play <b>Demon </b>again...)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T14:54:40-08:00","id":1469767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1469719-dtd-what-are-your-house-rules?p=1469760#post1469760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Been a while since I ran <b>Demon</b>, but I always capped the bonus on compromises you get for not using your forms at +5. It made the dice pool less unwieldy and a <i>tiny </i>bit more likely to fail. It also patches over an oddity that comes up where characters with Terrible Form are <i>really </i>good at handling partial transformation compromises.<br /> <br /> (Aaaand now I'm reading through the core and really want to play <b>Demon </b>again...)</div> </div> </div> </div>It always did seem odd that it broke the general rule of bonuses capping at +5. I never really thought about how terrible form could be used as a way to push that bonus even further. It definitely seems reasonable to nip such a thing before it gets out of hand.<br /> <br /> Also, ha, glad to get that interest sparked again. I wish you the best in finding a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T16:21:59-08:00","id":1469779,"title":"","content":"Mmm, now that I think of it I never gave a deep look at Demon\u2019s rules\u2026<br /> <br /> I heard that Mummy 2E has Kepher (\u2018Relic Sense\u2019) as a subset of the Investigstion system, and that Mage Sight in Mage 2E would\u2019ve been too. And Changeling 2E has Hedgespinning as a subset of the Chases system. Similar to these, I wonder how Social Maneuvering could work with Pacts, Chases with angels, the Conspiracy rules with Infrastructure and Cults, Investigations and Ephemeral Interactions with Cover, and so forth. (Or do they already? I have only a weak grasp on Demon atm\u2026)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T17:22:35-08:00","id":1469789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1469719-dtd-what-are-your-house-rules?p=1469760#post1469760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Aaaand now I'm reading through the core and really want to play <b>Demon </b>again...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I was starting a reread last night and had this exact same issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T18:04:19-08:00","id":1469791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1469719-dtd-what-are-your-house-rules?p=1469767#post1469767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It always did seem odd that it broke the general rule of bonuses capping at +5. I never really thought about how terrible form could be used as a way to push that bonus even further. It definitely seems reasonable to nip such a thing before it gets out of hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, for me it's kind of like, even though there's a <i>chance </i>of failure, anything above a +5 is basically not worth rolling. Statistically, you'll probably succeed. One could make the argument that it makes exceptional success more likely, and that offers a little bennie for characters who transform a lot, but I think a +5 offers that chance pretty well on its own. And some things do grant modifiers that exceed 5, but they're almost always supernatural. It's just that the ST can't throw out numbers greater than that arbitrarily.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, ha, glad to get that interest sparked again. I wish you the best in finding a game. </div> </div> </div>If the God-Machine wills it...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}